@@ -223,11 +223,11 @@ AFFORD-Bench organizes distribution shift into five levels:
 
 \textbf{L3: Visual ($\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{visual}}$).} Light intensity in $[0.5, 1.5]\,I_0$, light position jitter of $\pm 0.5\,\text{m}$, and object color jitter of $\pm 25\%$, leaving geometry unchanged.
 
-\textbf{L4: Physical ($\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{physics}}$).} Sliding friction $\mu \sim \mathcal{U}(0.12, 0.25)$ on $o^\star$ and on both finger pads, and mass and rotational inertia of $o^\star$ scaled by $\mathcal{U}(1.8, 2.5)$, at identical visual coordinates. MuJoCo takes the larger friction of a contact pair, so pads and body are set together. In a probe with the oracle's grasp shifted 10--20\,mm along the hand's lateral axis, lifted 10\,cm, and carried 20\,cm at the speed cap (3 seeds per setting), L4 dropped 8 of 12 off-center grasps of a cube and a mug, against 0 of 12 at nominal; centered grasps of the same bodies were held but slid 3--13\,mm, and the 24\,mm shaft was dropped at L4 even when grasped centrally.
+\textbf{L4: Physical ($\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{physics}}$).} Sliding friction $\mu \sim \mathcal{U}(0.12, 0.25)$ on $o^\star$ and on both finger pads, and mass and rotational inertia of $o^\star$ scaled by $\mathcal{U}(1.8, 2.5)$, at identical visual coordinates. MuJoCo takes the larger friction of a contact pair, so pads and body are set together. In a probe with the oracle's grasp shifted 10--20\,mm along the hand's lateral axis, lifted 10\,cm, and carried 20\,cm at the speed cap (3 seeds per setting), L4 dropped 8 of 12 off-center grasps of a cube and a mug, against 0 of 12 at nominal; centered grasps of the same bodies were held but slid 3--13\,mm, and under MuJoCo's default pyramidal friction cone ($\text{impratio}=1$) the 24\,mm shaft was dropped at L4 even when grasped centrally, whereas elliptic friction cones ($\text{impratio}=10$) hold centered shaft and mug grasps ($<5$\,mm slip) while dropping 20\,mm off-center grasps.
 
 \textbf{L5: Compound ($\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{comp}}$).} L2, L3, L4, and color shifts sampled jointly, combined with the multi-step instructions of D5--D7.
 
-\textbf{Physics and implementation.} All five levels are implemented. Lights, colors, friction, and masses are restored to nominal before each sample, and all sampling is seeded per episode. Grasping is frictional: the arm is driven by gravity-compensated joint position servos, the gripper is a force-limited tendon actuator, finger pads use stiff contacts (4\,ms time constant), and collisions use MuJoCo's native convex collision with multi-point contact. At reset, bodies are lifted out of any interpenetration and simulated to rest before the first observation.
